title: user:tag-remove
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Remove a tag from the selected metarecord

`user:tag-remove <tag|negative_tag|mixed_tag> <tag>` takes a tag off the selected metarecord: it asks which field of the tag model ([[Hierarchical tags]]), then which tag, completing over the ones the record has in that field, named by their paths. It runs [[metarecord:field]] `remove` with the tag entry's uuid, so it acts on the metarecord the [[metarecord-detail panel]] shows, and a path typed instead of picked is read like any value of that field ([[Ref value seeds]]). It rewrites nothing else: unlike [[user:tag-add]], a removal implies nothing about the other tags. The keys are `# d t`, `# d n` and `# d m` ([[Tagging from the GUI]]). An example of the shipped `commands.js`, to edit or delete ([[User commands]]).
